      "mergeID": "5ad99b38a575011d37d8b239",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Have the ability to stream audio from external audio services. Better alternative to me than hiding a webpannel underground or embedding the audio file right into the world in some cases.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Soundcloud/audio steaming",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a78909ab4e7a8489ff372d7",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "i was about to post another audio streaming request, but i'll just add to yours.  i think bandcamp is another great option, although it would be good to use any audio source.  what is needed also is a way to stream music so that you can sync it, so that when you walk into a virtual club for instance, you hear the music everyone else hears.  the best option now is to force people to download all the tracks before they get in, and even then it'll be silent before the next track starts.  much better if it was possible to just stream it and then you could also switch it up while keeping the same id.  it'd be way easier to vary the music from day to day, and hopefully in sync.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
